.TH HSH 1 "03 Sept 2026" "1.0" "Holberton School Shell Manual"

.SH NAME
hsh - holberton shell, simple UNIX holberton command language interpreter

.SH SYNOPSIS
hsh

.SH DESCRIPTION
hsh is a simplified version of a UNIX-like command interpreter (shell). It is implemented by compiling the files found in [Holberton Simple Shell Repository](https://github.com/DziRare/holbertonschool-simple_shell). Must be compilied in a valid UNIX-like shell. There are two ways to run the shell. In interactive and non-interactive mode. For interactive mode start the shell with ./hsh and enter any commands or executable /bin files to run along with their arguments. For non-interactive mode, run echo "{command and arguments}" | ./hsh.

.SH OPTIONS
There are no additional arguments or options for hsh.

.SH EXAMPLES
Interactive Mode:

school@holbertonschool-simple-shell:/# ./hsh

╚( ⚆ ⌂ ☉)╝ ls

ABOUT yasmin_file zac_file jonathan_file brendan_file sebastion_file uliana_file aladar_file munya_file hsh


Non-Interactive Mode:

school@holbertonschool-simple-shell:/# echo "ls" | ./hsh

ABOUT yasmin_file zac_file jonathan_file brendan_file sebastion_file uliana_file aladar_file munya_file hsh

